              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for an ointment, then the Hindi for a herbal brew."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: छाला",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छाला — chālā — \"a blister from rubbing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नए जूतों से मेरे पैर में छाला पड़ गया। nae jūtoṁ se mere pair meṁ chālā paṛ gayā. My new shoes gave me a blister on my foot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छाला (chālā) is inherited: CDIAL lists Hindi chālā, with the sense \"skin, hide\", under Sanskrit challi, \"bark\" (CDIAL 5005), beside chālī, \"a small blister\". The \"blister\" sense of chālā itself, skin lifted from the flesh, is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
